  "final_agent_text": "READY_TO_MODEL\n\nConfirmed understanding:\n\n- **Problem type:** Scheduling 5 fabric-dyeing batches on 3 dyeing vats to minimize the makespan (completion time of the last batch).\n- **Assignment:** Each batch must be assigned to exactly one vat and processed entirely there (no splitting across vats).\n- **Machines:** Each vat is a single machine that processes one batch at a time; no parallelism within a vat.\n- **Availability:** All 5 batches are available at time 0 (no release times).\n- **Sequencing:** Batches can be sequenced in any order on each vat (no fixed precedence).\n- **Setup:** No setup or changeover time between consecutive batches on a vat; the next batch starts immediately when the previous one finishes.\n- **Capacity:** No limit on how many batches a vat can take.\n- **Objective:** Minimize the makespan only; no other costs or penalties.\n- **Processing times (batch i, vat j):**\n  - Batch 1: [3, 1, 1]\n  - Batch 2: [2, 1.5, 1]\n  - Batch 3: [3, 1.2, 1.3]\n  - Batch 4: [2, 2, 2]\n  - Batch 5: [2.1, 2, 3]\n\nThis is a classic **P||Cmax** (unrelated parallel machines, makespan minimization) problem. I will formulate it as a mixed-integer program with binary assignment variables and sequencing (precedence) variables per vat, minimizing the maximum completion time.",
